    ;; Authority for this action lives in the update itself: the privileged
    ;; instruction validates its authorizations against the registry's own
    ;; governance and refuses otherwise. Requiring the configuration key here in
    ;; addition would let that one key block updates the registry authorized,
    ;; which is the single point of authority this design removes.
